{
 "node": "SpatialSound",
 "mode": "scene",
 "note": "the node's gain stage (intensity 0..1 times gain, stereo explicit) and the Web Audio panner (distance model and rolloff, with LINEAR held to rolloff 1, reference and maximum distance, cone angles from radians to degrees held to 0..360, cone outer gain, HRTF or equal power) are compared with X_ITE 16.6.0, and so is the panner's position and orientation: location and direction taken through the Transform and the camera (a viewpoint at 0 0 10) into view space. Runs in the real Babylon body. The panned sound is not compared.",
 "gaps": [
  "a SpatialSound plays only while it is drawn in X_ITE (its traversed flag, which a Switch or culling turns off); the bridge plays it whenever it is enabled",
  "spatialize is an initializeOnly field: set at load, bypassing the panner; the routing is not read back",
  "dopplerEnabled and priority are held; Web Audio has no doppler and there is one voice per node",
  "a maxDistance of 0 or less is refused by Web Audio (RangeError): the old distance stays; X_ITE 16.6.0 raises the error inside its event handler, so the test does not try it"
 ],
